# Analyst Notes

Registry enumeration is a common reconnaissance technique used by adversaries to understand the target environment before executing additional attack stages. Attackers often inspect registry locations to identify installed software, operating system configuration, antivirus products, startup entries, and persistence mechanisms.

Although registry queries are legitimate administrative operations, repeated enumeration of security-related or persistence-related registry paths should receive additional scrutiny, especially when combined with PowerShell execution, scheduled task creation, service manipulation, or registry modification events.

This detection complements Detection 10 (Registry Modification) by providing visibility into reconnaissance activity before configuration changes occur.
